A traditional New England blueberry buckle: a dense, rich buttermilk coffee cake bursting with fresh blueberries, weighted down by an irresistible layer of buttery cinnamon streusel that "buckles" the cake as it bakes.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a27920478/blueberry-buckle-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

### Cinnamon Streusel Crumble
- ½ cup all-purpose flour
- ⅓ cup granulated sugar
- 4 tablespoons unsalted butter, melted
- 1 teaspoon ground cinnamon
- Pinch kosher salt

### Blueberry Cake
- 2 cups all-purpose flour
- 2 teaspoons baking powder
- ½ teaspoon kosher salt
- 4 tablespoons unsalted butter, softened to room temperature
- ½ cup granulated sugar
- ¼ cup packed light brown sugar
- 1 large egg
- 2 teaspoons pure vanilla extract
- 1 cup buttermilk
- 2 cups fresh blueberries

## Instructions

1. **Get the Oven & Pan Ready:** Heat your oven to 375°F (190°C). Lightly coat an 8x8-inch metal or glass baking dish with nonstick spray, then line it with parchment paper leaving a slight overhang along the sides to easily lift the squares after baking.
2. **Blend the Cinnamon Crumb Topping:** In a mixing bowl, stir together the ½ cup flour, ⅓ cup sugar, melted butter, cinnamon, and salt using a fork until moist, crumbly pebbles form with no dry pockets of flour left behind. Set this streusel aside.
3. **Whisk the Dry Foundation:** In a medium bowl, whisk together the 2 cups of flour, baking powder, and ½ teaspoon salt to evenly distribute the leavener.
4. **Cream the Sugar and Butter:** In a larger bowl, beat the softened butter, granulated sugar, and brown sugar on medium speed until smooth and creamy. Beat in the whole egg and vanilla extract until fully unified.
5. **Form the Batter:** With a spoon or spatula, alternate folding in portions of the dry flour mixture and splashes of the buttermilk into the creamed butter, beginning and ending with dry ingredients. Stir just until the flour disappears—the batter will be notably thick and rich.
6. **Fold Blueberries and Layer:** Gently tumble the fresh blueberries into the thick batter using a rubber spatula, taking care not to burst them. Spoon into the lined dish and spread evenly into the corners. Evenly distribute the prepared streusel crumble across the top layer.
7. **Bake Until Golden:** Place on the center oven rack and bake for 40 to 45 minutes. The buckle is finished when the crumb topping is toasted and fragrant, and a wooden skewer poked into the middle emerges clean without wet crumbs.
8. **Rest and Slice:** Let the buckle settle in its pan on a wire rack for at least 15 to 20 minutes before cutting into nine generous squares.

## Notes

- **Fresh vs. Frozen Blueberries:** Fresh blueberries work best. If using frozen berries, do not thaw them prior to folding in; toss them with 1 tablespoon of flour first to prevent colors from bleeding into the batter.
